.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Organization | A customer | `northfield-university` |
    | Tenant | Same as Organization, used when talking about keeping data apart | Northfield and Acme |
    | Twin | The 3D copy of a real building | The 3D Science Hall |
    | Reading | One value from one room at one moment | Lab 2, 14:05, 27 °C |
    | Limit | The range a value should stay in | 18 to 26 °C |
    | Breach | The time a room spends outside a limit | Lab 2, from 14:05 to 14:20 |
    | Alert | The message sent for one Breach | "Lab 2 is too hot" |
    | Pass | Statement of who you are and your memberships | Lia's pass |
    | News | "This happened", sent to whoever listens | Breach Started |

.box {Two words to keep apart} type:{warning}
    - **Domain** in this chapter: one area of the business, like Alerting. The six are listed below.
    - **Organization**: a customer, like a university. The rest of the guide and the code call this a "Domain" too. Here it is always "Organization".

---

## The story, in six questions

Everything comes from six questions. Each one needs the answers before it, so the order is not random.

| # | Question | Domain | Needs |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Who are you, and what may you do? | [Identity & Access](domain-identity.qd) | Nothing |
| 2 | What does the place look like? | [Building Management](domain-buildings.qd) | 1, to know whose building it is |
| 3 | What is happening in each room, and is it OK? | [Telemetry Ingestion](domain-ingestion.qd) | 2, a reading needs a room |
| 4 | How do people follow a building, live? | [Telemetry Distribution](domain-distribution.qd) | 3, something to follow |
| 5 | Who must be told, and where? | [Alerting](domain-alerting.qd) | 1, 2 and 3 |
| 6 | Can someone explain all this to me? | [Knowledge & Assistance](domain-assistance.qd) | 1, 2 and 3 |

Click through the map, or read the pages in this order.

.mindmap center:{CrowdVision}
    - [1. Identity & Access](../docs/domain-model/domain-identity.qd)
        - Who are you?
    - [2. Building Management](../docs/domain-model/domain-buildings.qd)
        - What does the place look like?
    - [3. Telemetry Ingestion](../docs/domain-model/domain-ingestion.qd)
        - What is happening? Is it OK?
    - [4. Telemetry Distribution](../docs/domain-model/domain-distribution.qd)
        - How do people follow it?
    - [5. Alerting](../docs/domain-model/domain-alerting.qd)
        - Who must be told?
    - [6. Knowledge & Assistance](../docs/domain-model/domain-assistance.qd)
        - Can you explain it?

---

## How the domains talk

Three ways, and only three.

- **The pass.** Identity & Access gives each person a pass: who they are, and their role in each organization. Every domain trusts it.
- **News.** A domain says "this happened" and does not care who listens.
- **A question.** One domain asks another for something only that domain knows.

.mermaid
    flowchart LR
        B["2 Building Management"]
        T["3 Telemetry Ingestion"]
        D["4 Telemetry Distribution"]
        A["5 Alerting"]
        K["6 Knowledge & Assistance"]

        B -- "Building Ready" --> T
        B -- "Building Ready" --> D
        T -- "Reading Recorded, Breach Started, Breach Ended" --> D
        T -- "Breach Started" --> A
        A -. "which organizations?" .-> B
        K -. "what is this building?" .-> B
        K -. "what is happening?" .-> T

Solid arrow: news. Dotted arrow: a question. Identity & Access is left out because everyone holds its pass.

### All the news

| News | Said by | Heard by | What the listener does |
|---|---|---|---|
| Building Ready | Building Management | Ingestion, Distribution | Set starting limits, set starting Focus |
| Reading Recorded | Telemetry Ingestion | Distribution | Update the building's status |
| Breach Started | Telemetry Ingestion | Alerting, Distribution | Tell people, mark the room |
| Breach Ended | Telemetry Ingestion | Distribution | Mark the room as back to normal |

### All the questions

| Who asks | Who answers | Question | Why ask |
|---|---|---|---|
| Alerting | Building Management | Which organizations own this building? | Ownership is a Building Management fact, and an alert must never reach the wrong tenant |
| Knowledge & Assistance | Building Management | What is this building? | The assistant owns no facts |
| Knowledge & Assistance | Telemetry Ingestion | What is happening right now? | Same |

---

## One full example

Made-up numbers, used on every page of this chapter.

- **Organization:** `northfield-university`
- **Building:** Science Hall
- **Room:** Lab 2, temperature limit 18 to 26 °C
- **People:** Ada (Domain Administrator), Sam (Staff Member), Lia (Standard User)

Sam has a phone and a tablet. At 14:00 the lab is 25 °C. At 14:05 it reaches 27 °C.

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        participant S as Sensor in Lab 2
        participant T as Telemetry Ingestion
        participant D as Telemetry Distribution
        participant A as Alerting
        participant B as Building Management
        participant P as Sam

        S->>T: 14:00, 25 °C
        Note over T: recorded, inside 18 to 26
        T-->>D: Reading Recorded
        Note over D: Lia and Sam see 25 °C
        S->>T: 14:05, 27 °C
        Note over T: recorded, above 26, breach starts
        T-->>D: Reading Recorded
        T-->>A: Breach Started
        A->>B: Who owns Science Hall?
        B-->>A: northfield-university
        Note over A: Sam opted in to temperature alerts
        A->>P: alert on phone and tablet
        S->>T: 14:10, 27.5 °C
        Note over T: still above, same breach, no new alert
        S->>T: 14:20, 25 °C
        Note over T: back inside, breach ends
        T-->>D: Breach Ended

What to notice:

- Ingestion knows about the limit, not about Sam.
- Alerting knows about Sam, not about what 26 °C means.
- Following a building and being told are separate. Sam is told even if nobody is following.
- 14:05 and 14:10 are two readings but one problem, so one alert.

---

## Rules that hold everywhere

1. **One owner per fact.** A room's size lives in Building Management. Its temperature lives in Telemetry Ingestion. Nobody keeps their own copy of the truth.
2. **An organization is known by its name.** The name is the only thing all domains share.
3. **Tenants never see each other.** This holds in every domain.
4. **What happened stays recorded.** A wrong reading is fixed by a new reading, never by an edit.

---

## How much care each domain gets

Not every domain deserves the same effort.

| Kind | Meaning | Domains |
|---|---|---|
| Core | The reason customers pay | Building Management, Telemetry Ingestion, Telemetry Distribution |
| Supporting | Needed, but nobody picks us for it | Identity & Access, Alerting, Knowledge & Assistance |

---

## Not in this model

Left out for now:

- Sending commands to devices, like turning a boiler up.
- Knowing where each person is inside a building.
- Billing and subscriptions.
